population-pyramid-explorer — economic-lens backtest: data attribution (evals/econ/)
Written 2026-09-04. Applies to everything under evals/econ/ and to web/src/data/econ.json.

SHIPPED / REDISTRIBUTED (all CC BY 4.0; derived tables under evals/econ/tables/ and the site's econ file are built from these):

1. Maddison Project Database, version 2023.
   Bolt, Jutta and Jan Luiten van Zanden (2024), "Maddison style estimates of the evolution of the world
   economy: A new 2023 update", Journal of Economic Surveys, 1–41. https://doi.org/10.1111/joes.12618
   Data: Groningen Growth and Development Centre, https://www.rug.nl/ggdc/historicaldevelopment/maddison/releases/maddison-project-database-2023
   (file: DataverseNL 421302, sheet "Full data"; columns used: countrycode, year, gdppc, pop). Licence: CC BY 4.0.

2. Penn World Table version 11.0.
   Feenstra, Robert C., Robert Inklaar and Marcel P. Timmer (2015), "The Next Generation of the Penn World
   Table", American Economic Review, 105(10), 3150–3182, available for download at www.ggdc.net/pwt
   (PWT 11.0 release, 2025; file pwt110.xlsx, sheet "Data"; columns used: countrycode, year, rgdpna, rgdpe, pop).
   Licence: CC BY 4.0.

3. World Bank, World Development Indicators (WDI), accessed via the World Bank Indicators API v2
   (https://api.worldbank.org/v2/). Indicators used: NY.GDP.PCAP.PP.KD, NY.GDP.MKTP.KD.ZG, SP.POP.TOTL,
   SP.POP.1564.TO.ZS, NY.GDP.TOTL.RT.ZS. Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0),
   https://datacatalog.worldbank.org/public-licenses#cc-by (licence page to be re-verified and this line
   updated with the access date at M5.0, per docs/PLAN.md §7).

4. United Nations, Department of Economic and Social Affairs, Population Division (2024). World Population
   Prospects 2024, Online Edition (medium variant) — population totals used for the ≥ 1 M candidate floor
   and every pyramid shape. Licence: CC BY 3.0 IGO. https://population.un.org/wpp/

NEVER REDISTRIBUTED:

- IMF World Economic Outlook (April 2025) is read at build time only as a tail-year sanity check; no WEO
  value is written to evals/econ/tables/, to web/public/data/ or to web/src/data/econ.json
  (guarded by test_econ_export: nothing shipped matches /weo|imf|msci/i as a data source).
- MSCI index data are never downloaded as series. evals/econ/msci_citations.yaml contains only
  hand-transcribed facts (an annualised return, a drawdown, a base date) with the factsheet URL and the
  access date, cited as facts, exactly as a footnote would.
- ETF price data (Yahoo Finance chart API, daily adjusted closes) are fetched into data/raw/etf/
  (gitignored) and used ONLY to derive summary statistics (window log returns, CAGR, maximum drawdown,
  liveness checks). No price series, bar, or quote is committed, shipped, or displayed; the site shows
  derived statistics with the derivation date. Fund names and tickers are used nominatively to identify
  what exists or existed; nothing on the site is investment advice or a forecast.

